/-
# Simple groups generated by elements of orders 2 and 3 (Kourovka Notebook Problem 4.60)

Kourovka Notebook, Archive of Solved Problems, Problem 4.60 (D. M. Smirnov): (P. Hall) what is the
cardinality of the set of simple groups generated by two elements, one of order `2` and the other of
order `3`?
-/

module

public import Batteries.Util.ProofWanted
public import Mathlib.GroupTheory.OrderOfElement
public import Mathlib.GroupTheory.Subgroup.Simple

@[expose] public section

namespace MathlibExt.GroupTheory.SimpleTwoThreeGeneratedCardinalityKourovka4Problem60Wanted

/-!
Source: E. I. Khukhro and V. D. Mazurov (eds.), Unsolved Problems in Group Theory: The Kourovka
Notebook, 21st issue, arXiv:1401.0300v49 (2026), Archive of Solved Problems, Problem 4.60 (D. M.
Smirnov). UnsolvedMath record UM-00700267 (`KOU-4.60`), dataset ulamai/UnsolvedMath v1.8.0.

Groups are counted up to isomorphism. "Cardinality of the continuum" is stated as a bijection
between the subsets of `ℕ` and the isomorphism classes: a family `(S_t)_{t ⊆ ℕ}` of simple groups
generated by an element of order `2` and an element of order `3`, pairwise non-isomorphic, such that
every such group in `Type` is isomorphic to some `S_t`.
-/

/-- `S` is a simple group generated by an element of order `2` and an element of order `3`. -/
def IsSimpleTwoThreeGenerated (S : Type*) [Group S] : Prop :=
  IsSimpleGroup S ∧ ∃ x y : S, orderOf x = 2 ∧ orderOf y = 3 ∧ Subgroup.closure {x, y} = ⊤

/-- Kourovka 4.60 (P. Hall; D. M. Smirnov): the set of simple groups generated by an element of
order `2` and an element of order `3`, counted up to isomorphism, has the cardinality of the
continuum: its isomorphism classes are in bijection with the subsets of `ℕ` (a family `(S_t)`
indexed by `t ⊆ ℕ` of such groups, pairwise non-isomorphic, containing a copy of every such
group). -/
def simpleTwoThreeGeneratedContinuum : Prop :=
  ∃ (S : Set ℕ → Type) (_ : ∀ t, Group (S t)), (∀ t, IsSimpleTwoThreeGenerated (S t)) ∧
    (∀ t t', Nonempty (S t ≃* S t') → t = t') ∧
    ∀ (G : Type) [Group G], IsSimpleTwoThreeGenerated G → ∃ t, Nonempty (G ≃* S t)

/--
Resolved true: the Kourovka Archive answers 4.60 "The cardinality of the continuum": every
`2`-generated group embeds in a simple group generated by elements of orders `2` and `3` (Schupp),
such a group has at most countably many `2`-generator subgroups, and there are continuum many
`2`-generated groups (Merzlyakov). Source: E. I. Khukhro and V. D. Mazurov (eds.), Unsolved Problems
in Group Theory: The Kourovka Notebook, 21st issue, arXiv:1401.0300v49 (2026), Archive of Solved
Problems, Problem 4.60 (D. M. Smirnov); resolution: P. E. Schupp, Embeddings into simple groups, J.
London Math. Soc. (2) 13 (1976), no. 1, 90-94; Yu. I. Merzlyakov (1976), counting argument recorded
in the Kourovka Archive, Kourovka Archive of Solved Problems, Problem 4.60: The cardinality of the
continuum (every 2-generated group embeds in a simple group generated by elements of orders 2 and 3,
Schupp; such a group has at most countably many 2-generator subgroups, while there are continuum
many 2-generated groups, Merzlyakov 1976), https://doi.org/10.1112/jlms/s2-13.1.90.
-/
public theorem_wanted simpleTwoThreeGeneratedContinuum_holds : simpleTwoThreeGeneratedContinuum

end MathlibExt.GroupTheory.SimpleTwoThreeGeneratedCardinalityKourovka4Problem60Wanted
